    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0649" n="1483" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1483"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9696</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Netherland Chargé</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">De Beaufort</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 29, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge with
                    thanks the receipt of your note of April 23, 1918, with respect to the decision
                    of the Royal Government to send a convoy to the Dutch East Indies in June next,
                    for the purpose of relieving the personnel of the Ministry, transferring <pb
                        facs="0650" n="1484" xml:id="pg1484"/> Government officials and their
                    families and to carry military supplies for the colonial army.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
